# These files are test fixtures, and several of them test the container rather than
# the geometry: truncated.stl is a body cut short, trailing.stl is a valid body plus
# exactly one byte, and the binary STL reader decides a file is binary by comparing
# its size to 84 + 50 * triangleCount. Line-ending conversion would change those
# sizes and quietly turn the fixtures into something else, so it is switched off for
# the whole directory.

*.stl binary
*.obj -text
*.py  -text
*.abc3d binary
